From: kanoyami <secpro@foxmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: cgroup-v1: allow CAP_SYS_NICE to attach tasks

Android's system_server runs as UID 1000 with CAP_SYS_NICE (without
CAP_SYS_ADMIN) and moves application tasks across cgroup v1 hierarchies
(/dev/cpuctl, /dev/cpuset, /dev/blkio) via libprocessgroup. On mainline
Linux, __cgroup1_procs_write() rejects non-root cross-UID moves with
-EACCES unless CAP_SYS_NICE is accepted alongside UID matching.

Check CAP_SYS_NICE against the file-open credentials (of->file) in the
target task's user namespace, matching Android GKI while preserving
protection against inherited-fd attacks.

--- a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
@@ -523,7 +523,8 @@
 	tcred = get_task_cred(task);
 	if (!uid_eq(cred->euid, GLOBAL_ROOT_UID) &&
 	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->uid) &&
-	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->suid))
+	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->suid) &&
+	    !file_ns_capable(of->file, tcred->user_ns, CAP_SYS_NICE))
 		ret = -EACCES;
 	put_cred(tcred);
 	if (ret)
